# Next.js & React Patterns

## API routes — named exports, never default

All API route handlers in `src/app/api/` must use named HTTP method exports. Default exports are not used.

```typescript
// Correct
export const GET = withOptionalAuth(async (request, context) => { ... });
export const POST = withAgent(async (request, context) => { ... });
export const PATCH = withAuth(async (request, context) => { ... });
export const DELETE = withAdmin(async (request, context) => { ... });

// Wrong
export default async function handler(request) { ... }
```

## Protected API routes — always wrapped

Every route that requires authentication must be wrapped in a guard HOC before export. There must be no manual cookie/token reading in route handler bodies.

```typescript
// Correct
export const POST = withAgent(handler);

// Wrong — manual auth in handler body
export async function POST(request: NextRequest) {
  const token = request.cookies.get('access_token');
  // ...
}
```

## Client data fetching — hooks only

Pages and components must never use raw `fetch()` or `axios` directly. All data fetching and mutations go through TanStack Query hooks in `src/hooks/api/`.

```typescript
// Correct
const { data, isLoading } = useListings({ status: 'available' });

// Wrong
useEffect(() => {
  fetch('/api/listings').then(r => r.json()).then(setListings);
}, []);
```

## Query keys — always from the factory

Always use `queryKeys` from `src/lib/query/keys.ts`. Never inline string arrays.

```typescript
// Correct
queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: queryKeys.listings.saved() });
queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: queryKeys.auth.me() });

// Wrong
queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['listings', 'saved'] });
```

## Component placement

| Type | Directory |
|------|-----------|
| shadcn/Radix UI primitives | `src/components/ui/` — no business logic |
| Cross-feature shared utilities | `src/components/shared/` |
| Layout chrome | `src/components/layout/` |
| Feature-specific | `src/components/listing/`, `src/components/admin/`, `src/components/reviews/`, etc. |
| Heavy client detail screens | `src/components/listings/ListingDetailClient.tsx` pattern |
| Auth-related UI | `src/components/auth/` |
| Provider wrappers | `src/components/providers/` |

`src/components/ui/` is reserved for shadcn-generated primitive components. Do not add business logic, API calls, or domain-specific props there.

## Toast notifications — sonner only

Use `toast` from `sonner` for all user feedback. Never use `alert()`, `confirm()`, or `window.confirm()`.

```typescript
import { toast } from 'sonner';

toast.success('Listing saved successfully');
toast.error('Failed to submit payment proof');
```

The `Toaster` is mounted once in `src/app/layout.tsx`.

## Optimistic updates

When implementing optimistic UI (as in `useUpdateProfile`), follow the TanStack Query pattern:

```typescript
onMutate: async (newData) => {
  await queryClient.cancelQueries({ queryKey: queryKeys.auth.me() });
  const previous = queryClient.getQueryData(queryKeys.auth.me());
  queryClient.setQueryData(queryKeys.auth.me(), (old) => ({ ...old, ...newData }));
  return { previous };
},
onError: (_err, _vars, context) => {
  queryClient.setQueryData(queryKeys.auth.me(), context?.previous);
},
onSettled: () => {
  queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: queryKeys.auth.me() });
},
```

## Auth-gated UI

Use the `useAuth()` hook from `AuthProvider` for checking auth state in components:

```typescript
import { useAuth } from '@/components/providers/AuthProvider';

const { user, isAuthenticated, isLoading } = useAuth();
```

For routes that must redirect unauthenticated users, either rely on the Edge middleware (for `/dashboard`, `/profile`, `/unlock` prefixes) or use `useRequireAuth` from `src/hooks/useRequireAuth.ts` for custom redirect logic.

## Server component metadata

The only server component in the app is `src/app/layout.tsx` and individual `page.tsx` files that export `generateMetadata`. The `'use client'` directive is absent on these. Do not add `'use client'` to layout or pages that generate metadata.

```typescript
// src/app/listings/[id]/page.tsx — server component, no 'use client'
export async function generateMetadata({ params }: PageProps): Promise<Metadata> { ... }
export default async function ListingDetailPage({ params }: PageProps) {
  return <ListingDetailClient listingId={id} />;
}
```

Heavy client logic (state, hooks, events) lives in `*Client.tsx` components imported into the page.

## Image handling

Use `next/image` (`Image`) for all images that are part of UI layout. The `next.config.ts` allows any HTTPS hostname via `remotePatterns`. When the image URL is user-submitted (Cloudinary), use `Image` with `fill` and a sized container.

Note: `.eslintrc.json` has `@next/next/no-img-element: off` — raw `<img>` tags are allowed but prefer `Image` for optimised loading.

## Animation

Use `framer-motion` for animations. Follow the existing pattern in dashboard pages:

```typescript
<motion.div
  initial={{ opacity: 0, y: 20 }}
  animate={{ opacity: 1, y: 0 }}
  transition={{ delay: 0.1 }}>
  ...
</motion.div>
```

